-- The WILDCARD sibling of `1554_ctor_overlay_oracle_control/` — same three-file graph,
-- same adverse load order, one token different: `import zzcfg.*` where the control
-- writes `import zzcfg.{Cfg, CZ}`.  The control pins the spelling the import-scoped
-- constructor overlay ALREADY covered (`UseGroup`); this file pins the spelling it did
-- NOT.
--
-- 🚨 WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS, since an all-clean oracle looks like a fixture that tests
-- nothing.  `importOverlayDecls` (compiler/types/typecheck.mdk) matched `UseGroup`
-- alone and let `UseWild` fall through its `_ _ _ = []` fallback, so `import m.*`
-- contributed NO import-scoped overlay for `m`'s constructors.  Which declaration a
-- constructor occurrence meant was then decided by bare-name first-match over the flat,
-- LOAD-ORDERED data universe — i.e. by import-clause order.  The three conditions
-- `1554_…`'s header enumerates all hold here too (the observable is a DIAGNOSTIC not a
-- value; the load order is ADVERSE, `aacfg` first and `zzcfg` second; and the `match`
-- reaches the ORACLE, which has no `applyCtorScopeOverrides` fifth layer above it).
--
-- EXPECTED RESULT, DERIVED BY HAND BEFORE ANY RUN (this corpus has NO regeneration
-- script — `sh test/capture_goldens.sh analyze_project` is a no-op for it — and its
-- `oracle.json` is hand-written and reviewed, precisely so a wrong engine answer cannot
-- become the permanent expected output):
--
--   `Cfg` in this file can only mean `zzcfg.Cfg`.  It is the sole `Cfg` this file
--   imports: the `aacfg` clause is a member list naming only the VALUE `aaf`, which
--   binds no type and no constructor, while `import zzcfg.*` brings every name `zzcfg`
--   exports into scope.  `zzcfg.Cfg`'s sole constructor is `CZ`, so the single-arm
--   `match` is EXHAUSTIVE.  `f v` is `7`, `aaf 1` is `1`, and every file in the graph
--   publishes ZERO diagnostics.
--
-- MEASURED, on a binary cold-built from sprint/ctor-identity @ c7c879b7 (i.e. before
-- the `UseWild` arm existed): this exact graph instead reported
-- `non-exhaustive match of 'Cfg'. Missing case: 'CA'` — a `W-NONEXHAUSTIVE` naming a
-- constructor this file cannot name, read out of `aacfg.Cfg` purely because `aacfg`
-- loads first.  Swapping the two import lines flipped the answer to clean, which is the
-- order-dependence `test/import_order_fixtures/usewild-exhaust-oracle-invariant/` pins
-- on the other axis.  This fixture pins the ABSOLUTE answer that gate cannot supply.
import aacfg.{aaf}
import zzcfg.*

v : Cfg
v = CZ

f : Cfg -> Int
f x = match x
  CZ => 7

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  let _ = println (f v)
  println (aaf 1)
